##SECTION:RECEIPT_ARCHITECTURE

RECEIPT ARCHITECTURE

Every canonical action generates a receipt. A receipt is not a log entry. It is a binding acknowledgment that a thing happened, who caused it, and what it produced. Receipts cannot be deleted. They can be amended with an amendment receipt.

Receipt schema:

{
  "id": "ELEM-YYYY-MM-DD-AXI-NNNN",
  "action": "string – what was done",
  "timestamp_utc": "ISO‑8601",
  "timestamp_zurich": "ISO‑8601+01:00",
  "steward": "did:axi:mohamed",
  "generated_by": "string – which system or person",
  "input_hash": "SHA‑256 of input",
  "output_hash": "SHA‑256 of output",
  "artifacts_produced": ["list of file IDs or element IDs"],
  "covenants_invoked": ["COV#xxx"],
  "dignity_result": "TRUE | FALSE | NOT_EVALUATED",
  "provisional": true,
  "signed": false,
  "signed_by": [],
  "amendment_of": null
}

Never‑Lose Loop (from Grand_Archive AXI DNA):
Every input → Receipt → Distill → Index → Recirculate (same turn)
Recirculate means: at least one live artifact is updated and the receipt records where the input landed.

Dual‑time rule:
All receipts carry both UTC and Europe/Zurich timestamps. This is not decoration. Jurisdiction and audit require it.

