##SECTION:AUDIT_TRAIL_FORMAT

AUDIT TRAIL FORMAT

The audit trail is the append‑only record of every dignity check, covenant check, and system action. It is the proof that the system has acted as it claimed to act.

Audit entry schema:

{
  "audit_id": "AUD-YYYY-MM-DD-NNNN",
  "timestamp_utc": "ISO‑8601",
  "timestamp_zurich": "ISO‑8601+01:00",
  "action_type": "dignity_check | covenant_check | generation | ratification | amendment | anomaly_detected | gap_opened | gap_closed",
  "triggered_by": "module_name | steward | donor_hash",
  "input_summary": "string (never raw donor data)",
  "result": "PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED | DEFERRED",
  "dignity_result": {
    "evaluated": true,
    "components_checked": ["WITNESSED", "RECEIVED", "NOT_DIMINISHED", "RETURNABLE"],
    "failed_components": [],
    "suggested_remedies": [],
    "trace_id": "UUID"
  },
  "covenant_violations": [],
  "artifacts_affected": [],
  "provisional": true
}

Integrity rules for the audit trail:

- Append only. No deletion.
- Every dignity_check failure produces a full dignity_audit_object.
- Every covenant violation opens a ticket in the gap registry unless already present.
- Audit entries are hashed in sequence. Each entry carries the hash of the previous entry (Merkle chain).
- The audit trail itself must appear in the manifest.

